#
# Conformance case: teleology/currency-freshness-guard.
#
# An action schema carries a logic:FreshnessGuard (a valid-time currency guard) on its
# precondition: the datum backing the precondition is relied upon only while its age —
# from logic:datumRecordedAt to a probe's logic:decisionTime — is within the
# logic:freshnessHorizon (here P3D). Two gate probes share the same schema, state, and
# datum but differ in decision time: the datum is 2 days old at probeFresh (within the
# horizon → logic:GateAdmitted) and 5 days old at probeStale (beyond the horizon →
# logic:GateUndetermined, NOT stale-but-used and NOT denied — the evaluator declines to
# gate on an out-of-date value). This is GMEOW's native generalization of a decision-rule
# currency annotation.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/currency-freshness-guard/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
